From 116f7e816e0106b0ebe2b1d6ae0cc01d4d98a479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:50:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] facilitator-local: fill payer and network in error
 responses, use spec codes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Error bodies of /verify and /settle hardcoded "payer": "" and
"network": "", and reported every on-chain or transport failure as the
non-spec code unexpected_error. x402 v2 requires network (§5.3.2, a CAIP-2 id),
describes payer as the payer's address (§5.3.2, §5.4.2), names the
human-readable field invalidMessage (§5.4.2) and lists unexpected_verify_error
and unexpected_settle_error (§9).

- FacilitatorLocalError carries an ErrorContext with the request's network and
  the payer, which scheme handlers can now report through the new
  X402SchemeFacilitator::payer (default: none, and payer is then omitted).
- VerifyRequest::network reads the network as the request writes it.
- The EIP-155 v2 exact handler reports the authorization's from address.
- /verify errors add invalidMessage (invalidReasonDetails stays for existing
  clients); unexpected_error becomes unexpected_verify_error or
  unexpected_settle_error depending on the endpoint.

HTTP status codes are unchanged.
